# ===========================================================================
#  ATIO Knowledge Base -- Full OWL/RDF Ontology
#  sti_atio: namespace  <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#>
#
#  Version:    0.8-draft (May 2026)
#  Changes from v0.7:
#    - Added sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot: time-stamped real-world state
#      of an innovation (readiness/adoption/geography at a point in time).
#      DISTINCT from InnovationVersion (which tracks record changes).
#      hasSnapshot / isSnapshotOf bridge Innovation to its snapshots.
#      Properties: snapshotValidAt, snapshotSource, snapshotReason,
#      snapshotReadinessLevel, snapshotAdoptionLevel,
#      snapshotAdoptionCountry, snapshotEstimatedUsers.
#    - Added sti_atio:claimSubject on FieldClaim → Innovation (explicit).
#      FieldClaims are about real-world properties but asserted by records.
#      hasFieldClaim on InnovationRecord = container/grouping link.
#      claimSubject on FieldClaim = semantic link to real-world subject.
#      Canonical values asserted directly on Innovation after resolution.
#
#  Changes from v0.6:
#    KEY ARCHITECTURAL CHANGE: real-world / information-object separation
#    - Introduced sti_atio:InnovationRecord (prov:Entity, foaf:Document)
#      as the information object describing a sti_atio:Innovation.
#    - sti_atio:Innovation is now a PURE real-world entity:
#        rdfs:subClassOf schema:Product, schema:Thing
#        NOT rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity (real-world things are not
#        PROV entities in the strict sense)
#    - All data-management properties moved to sti_atio:InnovationRecord:
#        curationStatus, accessLevel, publishedAt, lastUpdated,
#        allowAIUpdate, dataLicense, dataRights,
#        derivedFromExtracted, derivedFromSource, providedBySource,
#        hasFieldClaim, hasTaxonomyMapping, hasVersion,
#        hasTemporalValue, hasFieldQA, qaScore, qaFlag
#    - New linking property: sti_atio:isDescribedBy
#        rdfs:subPropertyOf foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf
#        domain: sti_atio:Innovation  range: sti_atio:InnovationRecord
#    - Inverse: sti_atio:describes
#        rdfs:subPropertyOf foaf:primaryTopic
#        domain: sti_atio:InnovationRecord  range: sti_atio:Innovation
#    - All inter-innovation semantic relations (family, bundle, related,
#      componentOf) remain on sti_atio:Innovation — they are real-world
#      relations between real-world things
#    - FieldClaim, TaxonomyMapping, InnovationVersion, FieldQA all now
#      have domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord (not Innovation)
#    - SPARQL inference rule updated to traverse the isDescribedBy link
#    - Added foaf: prefix declaration
#    - Farm Suite instance data updated in examples
#  Changes from v0.5:
#    - Namespace renamed from atio: to sti_atio:
#      URI: https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/atio#
#        → https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#
#    - sti_atio:Innovation rdfs:subClassOf schema:Product
#      (replaces approximate owl:equivalentClass schema:SoftwareApplication)
#    - Added schema:Product property alignments:
#      schema:brand, schema:manufacturer, schema:funding,
#      schema:countryOfOrigin, schema:category, schema:review,
#      schema:isRelatedTo, schema:isPartOf, schema:hasMerchantReturnPolicy
#    - sti_atio:DigitalInnovation rdfs:subClassOf schema:SoftwareApplication
#      (more precise alignment for digital/software innovations only)
#    - Added sti_atio:BundleRelation rdfs:subClassOf schema:ProductCollection
#      (loose alignment; BundleRelation retains its own typed properties)
#    - Documented why schema:ProductGroup is NOT used for InnovationFamily
#  Changes from v0.4:
#    - FieldClaim generalised to ALL taxonomy-valued fields that may
#      carry source-specific vocabularies or divergent values
#    - New marker property sti_atio:claimEligible (boolean) declared on each
#      sti_atio: ObjectProperty: true = FieldClaim mechanism applies;
#      false = field normalised at ingestion (no claim needed)
#    - Harmonised fields (country, region, language) marked
#      sti_atio:claimEligible false with rationale
#    - FieldSchemeUsage now applicable to any claim-eligible property
#    - Updated SPARQL inference rule (no change needed — already generic)
#    - Updated SHACL shape: generalised from readiness-only to all
#      sti_atio:MaturityScheme / sti_atio:AdoptionScheme / new sti_atio:TypeScheme etc.
#    - New scheme marker classes: sti_atio:InnovationTypeScheme,
#      sti_atio:ThematicAreaScheme, sti_atio:UseCaseScheme, sti_atio:ActorTypeScheme
#    - Added sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale for documentation
#  Changes from v0.3:
#    - Added sti_atio:FieldSchemeUsage class: links a DataSource to the
#      vocabulary scheme it uses for a specific RDF property
#    - Added sti_atio:usesSchemeForField, sti_atio:forProperty, sti_atio:usesScheme
#    - Added sti_atio:claimProperty (URI form of claimField) to FieldClaim
#    - Added sti_atio:inferredScheme to FieldClaim (populated by SPARQL rule)
#    - Added SPARQL CONSTRUCT rule for scheme inference
#    - Updated SHACL shape to use inferred scheme when explicit scheme absent
#    - Updated FieldClaim to prefer claimProperty (URI) over claimField (string)
#  Changes from v0.2:
#    - Replaced owl:unionOf range classes (sti_atio:MaturityLevel,
#      sti_atio:AdoptionOrUptakeLevel) with open range (skos:Concept)
#    - Framework registration via sti_atio:MaturityScheme / sti_atio:AdoptionScheme
#      marker classes -- adding a new framework requires only two triples,
#      no ontology edit (analogous to extensible attribute types in XML Schema)
#    - Removed constituent range sub-classes (sti_atio:ReadinessLevel,
#      sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel, sti_atio:AdoptionLevel) as range constraints;
#      kept them as documentary classes for VocBench concept typing
#    - Added SHACL shapes for open-world validation of scheme membership
#    - Added sh: prefix declaration
#    - Updated ontology versionInfo and priorVersion
#  Changes from v0.1:
#    - Merged sti_atio:readinessLevel + sti_atio:scalingLevelIDIA into one property
#    - Merged sti_atio:adoptionLevel similarly under one property
#    - Added ConceptScheme declarations for CGIAR-TRL, IDIA-stages, CGIAR-adoption
#    - Added cross-scheme skos:closeMatch alignment examples
#    - Deprecated sti_atio:scalingLevelIDIA (kept as owl:deprecated sub-property)
#  Status:     Draft for review
#  Owner:      FAO Office of Innovation (OIN)
#  Contact:    ATIO@fao.org
#
#  Six layers:
#    L1 -- Knowledge Layer        (public KG)
#    L2 -- KOS / Taxonomy Layer   (public KG)
#    L3 -- Pipeline / Provenance  (internal / partner)
#    L4 -- Versioning             (internal / partner)
#    L5 -- Multi-source Divergence (internal / partner)
#    L6 -- Access & Governance    (metadata public)
#
#  Design principle: semantic correctness first; data management second.
#  The Innovation entity is whole -- properties are not split into
#  "core" vs "annotation" entities. Field divergence and access control
#  are handled via the FieldClaim pattern and named graphs respectively.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  PREFIX DECLARATIONS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@prefix sti_atio: <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#> .
@prefix sti:     <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti#> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcat:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix foaf:    <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix org:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/org#> .
@prefix schema:  <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix adms:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#> .
@prefix vann:    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  ONTOLOGY DECLARATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:title "ATIO Knowledge Base Ontology"@en ;
    dcterms:description """Ontology for the Agrifood Systems Technologies and Innovations
    Outlook (ATIO) Knowledge Base, developed by the FAO Office of Innovation.
    Covers the full semantic model: innovations, families, bundles, organisations,
    data sources, provenance, versioning, multi-source field divergence,
    and access governance."""@en ;
    dcterms:creator <https://sti-portal.fao.org/orgs/fao-oin> ;
    dcterms:rights "© FAO 2026. Licensed under CC-BY 4.0 for the ontology schema itself." ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.8-draft-2026-05" ;
    owl:priorVersion <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/atio/0.4> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "atio" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://sti-portal.fao.org/pages/atio-knowledge-base> .


# ===========================================================================
#  LAYER 1 -- KNOWLEDGE LAYER (PUBLIC KG)
#  Real-world entities: innovations, families, bundles, organisations, sources
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L1.1  sti_atio:Innovation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:Innovation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A specific real-world agrifood technology, practice, process,
    policy instrument, or institutional arrangement that constitutes an innovation.
    Represents one implementation -- not an abstract type (see sti_atio:InnovationFamily).
    The central knowledge unit of the ATIO KB."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:Thing ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L1.0  Real-world / information-object bridge  (v0.7)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:InnovationRecord
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The information object (data record) describing a
    sti_atio:Innovation. Carries all data-management concerns:
    provenance, versioning, curation, access control, field claims, QA.

    sti_atio:Innovation is the real-world entity — pure semantic content.
    sti_atio:InnovationRecord is the information artifact — prov:Entity,
    foaf:Document. They are linked via sti_atio:isDescribedBy
    (subPropertyOf foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf).

    In Drupal/JoinUp this is the node--innovation entity.
    One innovation may be described by multiple records (one per source
    before curator merge; one published record after)."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:subClassOf foaf:Document ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:isDescribedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is described by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Links a sti_atio:Innovation (real-world thing) to its
    sti_atio:InnovationRecord (information object). Subproperty of
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf. The innovation is the primary topic of its record.
    One innovation may have multiple records before merge."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf ;
    owl:inverseOf sti_atio:describes ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:describes
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "describes"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Inverse of sti_atio:isDescribedBy. Links a record to its subject innovation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf foaf:primaryTopic ;
    owl:inverseOf sti_atio:isDescribedBy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# InnovationRecord data-management properties
# (moved from sti_atio:Innovation in v0.7)

sti_atio:recordPublishedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "record first published"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordLastUpdated
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "record last updated"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordCurationStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "curation status"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range sti_atio:CurationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordAccessLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "access level"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range sti_atio:AccessLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordAllowAIUpdate
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "allow AI update of record"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordDataLicense
    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "record data license"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:license ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range dcterms:LicenseDocument ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordDataRights
    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "record data rights"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:rights ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range dcterms:RightsStatement ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordAttributionRequired
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "attribution required"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordQAScore
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "record QA score"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordAIEnrichmentStamp
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "AI enrichment stamp"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:aiGeneratedDescription
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "AI-generated description"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Internal AI description — data artifact, not real-world property."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordDerivedFromExtracted
    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "record derived from extracted innovation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links InnovationRecord to its AIExtractedInnovation precursor."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordDerivedFromSource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "record derived from source record"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:recordProvidedBySource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "record provided by data source"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ; rdfs:range sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L1.0.E  InnovationSnapshot — real-world state over time  (v0.8)
#
#  DESIGN NOTE: DISTINCT from sti_atio:InnovationVersion:
#
#    InnovationVersion  (data layer, on InnovationRecord)
#      Tracks changes to the DATA RECORD: curation edits, re-ingestion,
#      AI enrichment updates. Subject is InnovationRecord.
#      Drupal equivalent: node revision (sparql_entity_storage stores
#      each Drupal revision as a separate named graph version).
#
#    InnovationSnapshot  (real-world layer, on Innovation)
#      Tracks changes to the REAL-WORLD STATE: readiness level improves,
#      adoption spreads to new countries, user base grows, new impact
#      evidence emerges. Subject is Innovation.
#      Drupal equivalent: paragraph type 'innovation_snapshot' on the
#      node--innovation content type, or a dedicated content type
#      node--innovation_snapshot with entity reference back to
#      node--innovation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Snapshot"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A time-stamped representation of the known real-world
    state of a sti_atio:Innovation at a specific point in time.
    Captures values of key real-world properties as they were known or
    assessed at a specific date: readiness level, adoption level,
    adoption countries, estimated user base.

    DISTINCT from InnovationVersion (record versioning).
    InnovationSnapshot tracks real-world evolution;
    InnovationVersion tracks data record changes.

    Example: Innovation X was TRL-5 in 2022, TRL-7 in 2024, TRL-9 in 2026.
    Each assessment is an InnovationSnapshot.
    The corresponding InnovationVersions record who edited the database
    record when and which data fields were changed."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:hasSnapshot
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has snapshot"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links an Innovation to a time-stamped InnovationSnapshot of its real-world state."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    owl:inverseOf sti_atio:isSnapshotOf ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:isSnapshotOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is snapshot of"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:Innovation ;
    owl:inverseOf sti_atio:hasSnapshot ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:snapshotValidAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "snapshot valid at"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Date at which this snapshot was assessed or recorded."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:snapshotSource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "snapshot source"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The DataSource or curator Agent that produced this snapshot."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  prov:Agent ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:snapshotReason
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "snapshot reason"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Why this snapshot was created (e.g. new readiness evidence, new country adoption, periodic review)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:snapshotReadinessLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "readiness level at snapshot"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:snapshotAdoptionLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "adoption level at snapshot"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:snapshotAdoptionCountry
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "adoption countries at snapshot"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:snapshotEstimatedUsers
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "estimated users at snapshot"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationSnapshot ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.A  Identity & Core Description ---

sti_atio:innovationName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "innovation name"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The preferred name of the innovation. Note: many agrifood innovations
    do not have a single canonical name; alternative names are captured via
    schema:alternateName. AI-based duplicate detection addresses cases where
    different source records use different names for the same innovation."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:alternativeName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "alternative name"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Alternative or local name(s) under which the innovation is known."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:alternateName ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:shortDescription
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "short description"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A concise summary (approx. 100–200 words) of the innovation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:longDescription
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "long description"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Full narrative description of the innovation, covering mechanism,
    context, outcomes, and key dimensions. May be AI-generated if the source
    record lacks one (with data provider agreement)."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:aiGeneratedDescription
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "AI-generated description"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Internal AI-generated long description, used as a basis for
    field enrichment and chatbot prompts. Not always identical to the published
    long description. Stored in the internal named graph."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:identifyingFeature
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "identifying feature"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Narrative description of what makes this innovation recognisable
    and distinct from similar innovations -- used for deduplication and disambiguation."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:startYear
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "start year"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Year in which the innovation was first documented or implemented."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:gYear ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:startDate
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "start date"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Precise start date of the innovation (when available)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceURL
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source URL"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Canonical URL of the innovation record in its primary source system."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.B  Geography ---

sti_atio:originCountry
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "country of origin"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Country where the innovation was first developed or deployed."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Country ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:adoptionCountry
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "adoption country"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Country (or countries) where the innovation has been adopted
    or is actively used. Multi-valued."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Country ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:originRegion
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "region of origin"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "UN M49 or FAO geographic region of origin."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:GeographicRegion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:originCity
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "city of origin"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:originState
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "state / province of origin"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.C  Classification & Taxonomy References ---

sti_atio:innovationType
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "innovation type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Classification by functional domain and mechanism (e.g. precision
    agriculture, biological pest control, financial inclusion instrument).
    Multi-valued. References the ATIO innovation type taxonomy (SKOS)."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:innovationStage
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "innovation stage"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Lifecycle stage of the innovation (pre-emergent / emergent /
    mature / obsolete). References ATIO innovation stages taxonomy."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationStage ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:thematicArea
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "thematic area"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "FAO agrifood systems thematic area(s). Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:ThematicArea ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:challengeAddressed
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "challenge addressed"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Agrifood systems challenge(s) the innovation responds to. Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Challenge ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:useCase
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "use case"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Intended use case(s) or need(s) addressed by the innovation. Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:UseCase ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:useCaseNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "use case narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Free-text narrative describing the specific use case context."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mainUseCaseImage
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "main use case (for image selection)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The single use case selected as the primary label for image/icon display."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:UseCase ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:language
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "language"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Language(s) in which the innovation documentation or interface is available."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Language ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:farmingSystem
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "farming system"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Farming system classification(s) relevant to the innovation. Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FarmingSystem ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.D  Innovative Dimensions ---

sti_atio:innovativeFeature
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "innovative dimension"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The specific dimension(s) of innovativeness: what makes it
    novel relative to existing solutions. References ATIO innovative features
    taxonomy (built from FAO S&I Strategy innovation criteria). Multi-valued."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovativeFeature ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:innovativeFeaturesNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "innovative dimensions narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Free-text narrative elaborating the innovation's key novel dimensions."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:isGrassroots
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is grassroots innovation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Boolean flag indicating that this innovation originates from
    farmer-led, community-driven, or grassroots knowledge systems rather than
    formal R&D. Triggers special handling for attribution, consent, and governance."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.E  Readiness & Adoption ---

sti_atio:readinessLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "readiness level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """CGIAR Scaling Readiness level (0–9). An intrinsic property of the
    innovation reflecting evidence-based validation of its development stage.
    References ATIO readiness levels taxonomy aligned to CGIAR CLARISA."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:readinessNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "readiness narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Free-text justification or description of the assessed readiness level."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:adoptionLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "adoption level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """CGIAR 9-level adoption scale. Reflects the actual spread and uptake
    of the innovation in real-world use. References ATIO adoption levels taxonomy."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:adoptionNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "adoption narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Free-text description of the adoption context, evidence, and trajectory."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# sti_atio:scalingLevelIDIA -- v0.1 property, now deprecated.
# The v0.3 declaration (deprecated sub-property of sti_atio:readinessLevel)
# appears in the readiness/maturity property block above.
# This stub is removed; see the merged property block for the full declaration.

sti_atio:estimatedUsers
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "estimated number of users"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Best available estimate of actual current users or beneficiaries."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.F  Adoptability Dimensions ---
#  These are intrinsic properties of the innovation, not metadata.
#  They reflect dimensions specifically designed for the ATIO KB to capture
#  uptake-relevant information absent from most existing databases.

sti_atio:accessibility
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "accessibility"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Degree to which the innovation is accessible to target users
    in terms of cost, availability, and infrastructure requirements."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AdoptabilityLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:accessibilityNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "accessibility narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:acceptability
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "acceptability"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Degree to which the innovation is culturally, socially, and
    behaviourally acceptable to target users and communities."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AdoptabilityLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:acceptabilityNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "acceptability narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:profitability
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "profitability"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Degree to which the innovation is economically viable and
    profitable for target users."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AdoptabilityLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:profitabilityNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "profitability narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sustainability
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "sustainability"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Environmental and social sustainability of the innovation
    over its full lifecycle."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AdoptabilityLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sustainabilityNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "sustainability narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:coDevelopment
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "co-development"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Degree to which the innovation was co-developed with or by
    its target users (a key dimension of inclusivity and grassroots relevance)."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AdoptabilityLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:coDevelopmentNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "co-development narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.G  Actors ---

sti_atio:actualUser
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "actual user"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Actor type(s) that are currently using the innovation. Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:ActorType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:prospectiveUser
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "prospective user"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Actor type(s) identified as potential future users. Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:ActorType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:investmentType
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "investment type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Type(s) of investment required or involved in the innovation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InvestmentType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.H  Impact ---

sti_atio:impactSDG
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "impact: SDG"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """UN Sustainable Development Goal(s) that this innovation contributes
    to. References UN SDG URIs where available as dereferenceable LOD resources."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:SDGGoal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:impactFourBetters
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "impact: FAO Four Betters"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """FAO Four Betters dimension(s) addressed: better production,
    better nutrition, better environment, better life."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FourBetter ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:impactNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "impact narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Narrative description of the innovation's observed or expected impact."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.I  Grassroots-specific fields ---
#  Only populated for innovations where sti_atio:isGrassroots = true

sti_atio:communityOwner
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "community owner"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The community or grassroots organisation that holds knowledge
    rights over this innovation. Triggers attribution and consent requirements."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range org:Organization ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:communityConsent
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "community consent status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Status of informed consent from the community for knowledge publication."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:ConsentStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:grassrootsAssessment
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "grassroots assessment flag"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Indicates that the grassroots assessment was completed by an
    authorised grassroots partner focal point (displayed as a flag in search results)."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:localResourceBased
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "relies on local resources"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the innovation primarily uses locally available resources."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.J  Organisational Relationships ---

sti_atio:developedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "developed by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Organisation(s) that developed the innovation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range org:Organization ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ownedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "owned by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Organisation that claims intellectual property or management
    rights over the innovation."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range org:Organization ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:implementedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "implemented by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Organisation(s) currently implementing or deploying the innovation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range org:Organization ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:fundedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "funded by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Organisation(s) providing funding for the innovation's development or scaling."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range org:Organization ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.K  Family & Bundle Relations ---

sti_atio:memberOfFamily
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "member of family"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The innovation family (or families) to which this innovation belongs.
    Multi-valued: an innovation may belong to more than one family if it shares
    defining feature dimensions with multiple family abstractions."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:participatesInBundle
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "participates in bundle"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Bundle relation in which this innovation participates. Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:BundleRelation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.L  Provenance links (public subset) ---

sti_atio:derivedFromSource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "derived from source record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Shortcut provenance link to the original source record(s) from
    which this innovation was synthesised. Full provenance chain is available
    via the pipeline layer (sti_atio:derivedFromExtracted)."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:providedBySource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "provided by data source"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The data source (sti_atio:DataSource) from which the innovation originates."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:publishedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "first published date"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:lastUpdated
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "last updated"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:curationStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "curation status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Current editorial/workflow status of this innovation record."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range sti_atio:CurationStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- L1.1.M  Access & Rights (on the Innovation) ---

sti_atio:accessLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "access level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Governs visibility: public | partner-only | internal | embargoed."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AccessLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:dataLicense
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "data license"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "License under which this innovation record's data is shared."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:license ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:LicenseDocument ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:dataRights
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "data rights"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:rights ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:RightsStatement ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:attributionRequired
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "attribution required"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:attributionText
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "attribution text"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:allowAIUpdate
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "allow AI update"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Flag indicating whether the AI enrichment pipeline may overwrite
    fields in this record on future ingestion runs. When false, curated fields
    are protected ('do not overwrite by AI')."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L1.2  sti_atio:InnovationFamily
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:InnovationFamily
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Family"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A named analytical abstraction grouping multiple specific innovation
    implementations by shared mechanism, feature dimensions, or functional domain.
    NOT a taxonomy class or SKOS concept: families are dynamic named entities with
    temporal identity, split/merge history, and family-level analytics.
    They are the unit of analysis; innovations are the unit of information."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:Thing ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:familyName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "family name"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:familyDescription
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "family description"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Feature dimensions A–E (Ranganathan facets)
sti_atio:featureDimensionA
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "feature dimension A (mechanism)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Defining facet A: the core mechanism or mode of action."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:featureDimensionB
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "feature dimension B (domain)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Defining facet B: the functional or thematic domain."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:featureDimensionC
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "feature dimension C (target)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Defining facet C: target beneficiary or system component."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:featureDimensionD
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "feature dimension D (context)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Defining facet D: agroclimatic, geographic, or institutional context."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:featureDimensionE
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "feature dimension E (innovation form)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Defining facet E: form or modality of the innovation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Temporal identity
sti_atio:familyBirthDate
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "family birth date"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Date on which this family was first identified and registered."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:familyRegistryVersion
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "family registry version"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Version of the Family Registry methodology used when this family was defined."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:splitFromFamily
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "split from family"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The parent family from which this family was split."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mergedIntoFamily
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "merged into family"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The successor family into which this family was merged (when deprecated)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mergedFromFamily
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "merged from family"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A predecessor family that was merged to create this family."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:familyStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "family status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Current status of this family entity: active | deprecated | proposed."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FamilyStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Optional alignment to SKOS/OWL representation (see ADR-011)
sti_atio:correspondingConcept
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "corresponding KOS concept"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Optional: the SKOS concept in VocBench that corresponds to this
    family entity. Used when the family is also managed as a SKOS concept in the
    VocBench vocabulary management environment."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    owl:equivalentProperty skos:exactMatch ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L1.3  sti_atio:BundleRelation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:BundleRelation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Bundle Relation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A reified typed relation between two or more innovations that are
    complementary, interdependent, sequentially deployed, or frequently co-cited.
    Reification is semantically appropriate here: the bundle type and evidence are
    properties of the relation itself, not of either participating innovation."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:bundleType
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "bundle type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The type of complementarity linking innovations in this bundle."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:BundleRelation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:BundleType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:bundleMember
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "bundle member"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An innovation participating in this bundle relation. Multi-valued (≥2)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:BundleRelation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:bundleEvidenceType
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "bundle evidence type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "How this bundle relation was established."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:BundleRelation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:BundleEvidenceType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:bundleConfidenceScore
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "bundle confidence score"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "AI confidence score for AI-detected bundles (0.0–1.0)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:BundleRelation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:bundleCuratorConfirmed
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "curator confirmed"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether a human curator has confirmed this bundle relation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:BundleRelation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:bundleNarrative
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "bundle narrative"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Explanation of how and why these innovations are bundled."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:BundleRelation ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L1.4  sti_atio:DataSource   (extends dcat:Dataset)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:DataSource
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ATIO Data Source"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """An external database, platform, API, or information service
    from which the ATIO KB harvests or receives innovation data.
    Models the data source as an information resource (cf. dcat:Dataset),
    distinct from the organisation that manages it (org:Organization)."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf dcat:Dataset ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:trustLevel
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "trust level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust classification determining the QA approach applied to ingested content."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:TrustLevel ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:harvestingMethod
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "harvesting method"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Technical method used to harvest data from this source."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:HarvestingMethod ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:harvestingStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "harvesting status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Current operational status of the harvesting pipeline for this source."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:HarvestingStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sharingAgreement
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "data sharing agreement"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to or description of the data sharing agreement with this source."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:allowsAIEnrichment
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "allows AI enrichment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the data sharing agreement permits AI enrichment of harvested records."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:allowsPublicDisplay
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "allows public display"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether records from this source may be displayed in the public KB."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:fieldSharingScope
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "field sharing scope"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Policy defining which fields from this source may be published publicly."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FieldSharingScope ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceManagedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "managed by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Organisation(s) responsible for managing this data source. Many-to-many."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range org:Organization ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:lastHarvestedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "last harvested at"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:updateFrequency
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "update frequency"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:accrualPeriodicity ;
    rdfs:range dcterms:Frequency ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceAPIEndpoint
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "API endpoint"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceSchemaFormat
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source schema / format"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Schema or format of the data as delivered by this source (e.g. JSON, XML, CSV, RDF)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ===========================================================================
#  LAYER 2 -- KOS / TAXONOMY LAYER
#  All taxonomies are SKOS ConceptSchemes.
#  Concept instances are not defined here -- they are managed in VocBench.
#  Classes below are owl:Class declarations acting as rdfs:range targets,
#  each corresponding to one SKOS ConceptScheme.
# ===========================================================================

sti_atio:InnovationType     a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Concept in the ATIO Innovation Types taxonomy (functional domain + mechanism)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:InnovationStage    a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Stage"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Pre-emergent | emergent | mature | obsolete."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ThematicArea       a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thematic Area"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "FAO agrifood systems thematic area."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:Challenge          a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Challenge"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Agrifood systems challenge addressed by the innovation."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:UseCase            a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Use Case"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Intended use case or need addressed."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Maturity / Readiness -- union range class and constituent scheme classes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:MaturityLevel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Maturity / Readiness Level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Union range for sti_atio:readinessLevel. Any SKOS concept that is
    a member of a recognised readiness or scaling framework qualifies.
    Currently two constituent classes (one per supported scheme):
      sti_atio:ReadinessLevel   -- concepts in <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl>
      sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel -- concepts in <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages>
    The union is declared via owl:unionOf to allow OWL reasoners to
    validate that a referenced concept belongs to at least one scheme."""@en ;
    owl:unionOf ( sti_atio:ReadinessLevel sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel ) ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ReadinessLevel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sti_atio:MaturityLevel ;
    rdfs:label "CGIAR Readiness Level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A concept in the CGIAR Scaling Readiness 9-level scale
    (<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl>). Aligned to NASA TRL. Managed in VocBench."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sti_atio:MaturityLevel ;
    rdfs:label "IDIA Scaling Stage"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A concept in the IDIA 6-stage scaling continuum
    (<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages>). Suited to social, institutional, and
    policy innovations. Managed in VocBench."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Adoption / Uptake -- union range class and constituent scheme class
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:AdoptionOrUptakeLevel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Adoption / Uptake Level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Union range for sti_atio:adoptionLevel. Currently one constituent class
    (CGIAR adoption scale); extensible to additional frameworks via owl:unionOf."""@en ;
    owl:unionOf ( sti_atio:AdoptionLevel ) ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:AdoptionLevel
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sti_atio:AdoptionOrUptakeLevel ;
    rdfs:label "CGIAR Adoption Level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A concept in the CGIAR 9-level adoption scale
    (<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-adoption>). Managed in VocBench."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:AdoptabilityLevel  a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Adoptability Level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Ordinal level for adoptability dimensions (high/medium/low or 1–5 scale)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ActorType          a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Actor Type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Type of actor (smallholder farmer, extension agent, government, etc.)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:InvestmentType     a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Investment Type"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:InnovativeFeature  a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Innovative Feature"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Dimension of innovativeness per FAO S&I Strategy criteria."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:SDGGoal            a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "SDG Goal"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "UN Sustainable Development Goal. Aligned to UN SDG Linked Data URIs."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:FourBetter         a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "FAO Four Better"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "FAO Four Betters dimension: better production / nutrition / environment / life."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:Country            a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Country"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Country. Aligned to UN M49 and ISO 3166-1 alpha-3."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:GeographicRegion   a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Geographic Region"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "FAO/UN M49 geographic region or sub-region."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:Language           a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Language"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "BCP47 / ISO 639 language code."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:FarmingSystem      a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Farming System"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Enumeration classes (controlled values -- managed as SKOS concepts or OWL individuals)

sti_atio:BundleType         a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Bundle Type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "complementary | interdependent | sequential | co-cited"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:BundleEvidenceType a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Bundle Evidence Type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "AI-detected | curator-confirmed | partner-stated | use-case-overlap"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:TrustLevel         a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Trust Level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "trusted-partner | general-source | unvalidated"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:HarvestingMethod   a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Harvesting Method"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "API | file-import | scraping | crowdsourcing | manual-entry"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:HarvestingStatus   a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Harvesting Status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "active | paused | deprecated | pending-onboarding"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:CurationStatus     a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Curation Status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "draft | staged | published | archived | flagged"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:AccessLevel        a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Access Level"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "public | partner-only | internal | embargoed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:FamilyStatus       a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Family Status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "active | deprecated | proposed"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ConsentStatus      a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Consent Status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "obtained | pending | not-applicable | anonymised"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:FieldSharingScope  a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Field Sharing Scope"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "all-fields | core-only | custom-field-list | no-sharing"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:QAStatus           a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "QA Status"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "complete | incomplete | AI-generated | curator-curated | flagged | missing"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:MappingType        a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Taxonomy Mapping Type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "exactMatch | closeMatch | broadMatch | narrowMatch | noMapping"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:VersionTrigger     a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Version Trigger"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "new-ingestion-run | curator-edit | ai-enrichment | merge-event | source-update"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L1.5  sti_atio:FieldSchemeUsage  (v0.4)
#  Declares which vocabulary scheme a DataSource uses for a given RDF property.
#  Declared ONCE at data source onboarding; never repeated per innovation.
#  The inference rule in the SPARQL RULES section derives sti_atio:inferredScheme
#  on every FieldClaim produced from that source, without any repetition at
#  the individual claim level.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:FieldSchemeUsage
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Field Scheme Usage"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A declaration that a specific data source uses a specific
    vocabulary scheme for values of a specific RDF property.
    Declared once at onboarding on the sti_atio:DataSource node.
    Enables scheme inference on all sti_atio:FieldClaim nodes produced from
    that source for that property, without repeating scheme information
    at the individual claim level.

    Example: CGIAR Catalog uses cgiar-catalog/vocab/scaling-readiness
    for the sti_atio:readinessLevel property. Once declared, every FieldClaim
    originating from CGIAR Catalog records for readinessLevel automatically
    has its scheme resolved by inference."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:usesSchemeForField
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses scheme for field"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Links a DataSource to a FieldSchemeUsage declaration.
    Multi-valued: a source may use different schemes for different properties."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:FieldSchemeUsage ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:forProperty
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "for property"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The RDF property (by URI) for which the scheme usage is declared.
    Using the property URI (not a string name) enables clean SPARQL inference
    without string matching."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldSchemeUsage ;
    rdfs:range  rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:usesScheme
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "uses scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The skos:ConceptScheme that this data source uses for the
    declared property. Should ideally be typed as sti_atio:MaturityScheme or
    sti_atio:AdoptionScheme as appropriate; if not yet registered, the inference
    rule still fires but the SHACL shape will emit a warning."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldSchemeUsage ;
    rdfs:range  skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ===========================================================================
#  LAYER 3 -- PIPELINE / PROVENANCE LAYER
#  The three-stage ingestion model. Implements W3C PROV-O.
#  Primary named graph: <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#graph/provenance>
#  Accessible to: internal curators and authorised partners.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L3.1  sti_atio:SourceRecord
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:SourceRecord
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Source Record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The verbatim content of an innovation record as harvested or received
    from a data source. Never modified after initial storage. Versioned per
    harvesting run. The authoritative provenance anchor: every downstream
    entity traces back to a specific source record at a specific ingestion datetime.
    Implements prov:Entity."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:harvestedFrom
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "harvested from"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:DataSource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:harvestedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "harvested at"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:rawContent
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "raw content"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The verbatim content of the source record (JSON, XML, or plain text)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceRecordVersion
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source record version"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Version identifier for this snapshot of the source record."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceOriginalID
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source original ID"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The identifier of this record in the source system's own schema."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceOriginalURL
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source original URL"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceOriginalLanguage
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "original language"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Language ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:harvestingRunID
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "harvesting run ID"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Identifier of the harvesting pipeline run that produced this record."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L3.2  sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "AI-Extracted Innovation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The intermediate bridge entity produced by the AI enrichment pipeline.
    Holds all fields from the source record(s) plus AI-generated values for
    fields absent or incomplete in the source. May be linked to multiple source
    records (in multi-source merging scenarios). Acts as the buffer between
    raw ingestion and curated publication -- allowing enrichment experiments
    without affecting the published record.
    Implements prov:Entity derived from sti_atio:SourceRecord."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:extractedFromSource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "extracted from source record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The source record(s) from which this extracted innovation was derived. Multi-valued."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:extractionActivity
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "extraction activity"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasGeneratedBy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:aiExtractionVersion
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "AI extraction version"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Version identifier of the extraction run (date + prompt version)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:aiModelUsed
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "AI model used"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Identifier of the LLM or AI model used for enrichment (e.g. gemini-1.5-pro)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:aiPromptVersion
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "AI prompt version"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Version of the enrichment prompt template used."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mergeStrategy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "merge strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "How multiple source records were combined into this extracted entity."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:MergeStrategy ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:derivedFromExtracted
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "derived from extracted innovation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links the published innovation back to its AI-extracted precursor."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;  # moved from Innovation in v0.7
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:MergeStrategy      a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Merge Strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "AI-merge (many-to-one) | curator-merge (many-extracted-to-one-published)"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L3.3  sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity   (prov:Activity)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "AI Enrichment Activity"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A specific run of the AI enrichment pipeline processing one or more
    source records. Implements prov:Activity. The combination of agent (AI model),
    prompt version, and execution timestamp makes each enrichment activity
    deterministic and auditable."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:enrichmentAgent
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "enrichment agent"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The AI software agent (model + configuration) that performed the enrichment."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity ;
    rdfs:range prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasAssociatedWith ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:enrichmentStartedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "enrichment started at"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:startedAtTime ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:enrichmentEndedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "enrichment ended at"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:endedAtTime ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:inputSourceRecord
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "input source record"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:used ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L3.4  sti_atio:FieldProvenance  (per-field AI vs. source attribution)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:FieldProvenance
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Field Provenance"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Records whether a specific field value on a published innovation was
    taken directly from a source record, generated by AI, or manually curated.
    Attaches to individual field instances on the AIExtractedInnovation or Innovation."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:provenanceField
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "field name"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldProvenance ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:provenanceSource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "value source"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the field value came from the source record, AI generation, or curation."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldProvenance ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FieldValueSource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:FieldValueSource   a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Field Value Source"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "source-record | ai-generated | curator-added | ai-curated | default"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:provenanceActivity
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "generating activity"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldProvenance ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:hasFieldProvenance
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has field provenance"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FieldProvenance ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ===========================================================================
#  LAYER 4 -- VERSIONING
#  Record-level versioning and field-level temporal tracking.
#  Named graph: sti_atio:graph/provenance  (internal / partner)
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L4.1  sti_atio:InnovationVersion
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:InnovationVersion
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Version"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A timestamped snapshot of the state of a published innovation record.
    Created at every significant change: new ingestion run with updated source content,
    manual curator edit, AI enrichment update, or merge event. Implements prov:Entity."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:hasVersion
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has version"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links the current published innovation to its historical version snapshots."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:versionOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "version of"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Innovation ;
    owl:inverseOf sti_atio:hasVersion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:versionNumber
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "version number"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:versionCreatedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "version created at"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:versionCreatedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "version created by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Human curator (foaf:Person) or AI pipeline agent (prov:SoftwareAgent)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range prov:Agent ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:versionTrigger
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "version trigger"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "What caused this new version to be created."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:VersionTrigger ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:versionChangeSummary
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "change summary"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Human-readable description of what changed in this version."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:versionState
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "serialised state"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The full serialised state of the innovation record at this version
    (JSON snapshot), allowing full revert without re-querying the triple store."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:previousVersion
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "previous version"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:InnovationVersion ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L4.2  sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue  (field-level temporal tracking -- Phase 3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Field Temporal Value"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A timestamped historical value for a specific field on an innovation.
    Enables trend analysis of individual fields (readiness level trajectory,
    adoption spread over time, geographic reach evolution) independently of
    full record versioning. Planned for selective implementation in Phase 3
    for priority fields: readinessLevel, adoptionLevel, estimatedUsers, adoptionCountry."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:temporalField
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "field name"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:temporalFieldValue
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "field value"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The value of the field at the recorded time (literal or URI serialised as string)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:temporalFieldValueRef
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "field value (reference)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The value of the field at the recorded time, when it is an entity reference."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Resource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:validFrom
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "valid from"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:validTo
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "valid to"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "End of validity period. Absent = currently valid."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:temporalValueSource
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "value source"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Which ingestion run or curator action produced this temporal value record."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue ;
    rdfs:range prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:hasTemporalValue
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has temporal value"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FieldTemporalValue ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ===========================================================================
#  LAYER 5 -- MULTI-SOURCE DIVERGENCE
#  Field claims (different source records giving different values for the same
#  field) and taxonomy mapping divergence across source vocabularies.
#  Named graph: sti_atio:graph/provenance  (internal / partner)
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L5.1  sti_atio:FieldClaim
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:FieldClaim
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Field Claim"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A claim about the value of a specific field of an innovation,
    attributed to a specific source record. Allows multiple, potentially divergent
    claims on the same field of the same innovation from different source records
    to coexist. The canonical (published) value on sti_atio:Innovation is the
    curator-selected synthesis; sti_atio:FieldClaim preserves the full divergence
    for auditability, research, and re-ingestion.
    Semantically: a reified statement (cf. RDF reification / named graph pattern)."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:hasFieldClaim
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has field claim"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimSubject
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim subject"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimSubject
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim subject"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The real-world sti_atio:Innovation that this FieldClaim
    is about. Explicitly separates the semantic subject (Innovation) from
    the record that carries the claim (InnovationRecord).

    Both of the following hold simultaneously and serve different purposes:

      sti_atio:InnovationRecord --hasFieldClaim--> sti_atio:FieldClaim
        (grouping/container: which record is associated with this claim)

      sti_atio:FieldClaim --claimSubject--> sti_atio:Innovation
        (semantic: which real-world thing this claim is about)

    FieldClaims are reified property assertions: they sit in the data/
    provenance layer but their subject is a real-world entity. After
    curator resolution the canonical value is asserted directly on
    sti_atio:Innovation. The FieldClaim provides the evidence trail."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimField
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim field"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The field name to which this claim applies (e.g. 'readinessLevel', 'originCountry')."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimLiteralValue
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim value (literal)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The claimed field value when it is a literal (string, integer, date, etc.)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimRefValue
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim value (reference)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The claimed field value when it is an entity or concept reference (URI)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Resource ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claimed by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The source record that asserts this field value."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claimed at"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Timestamp at which this claim was extracted from the source record."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:curatorResolution
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "curator resolution"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "How the curator resolved this claim relative to others for the same field."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:ClaimResolution ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ClaimResolution    a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Claim Resolution"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "authoritative | supplementary | rejected | pending-review"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimResolutionNote
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "resolution note"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Curator note explaining the resolution decision."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimProperty
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim property (URI)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The RDF property to which this claim applies, expressed as a URI.
    Preferred over sti_atio:claimField (string) in v0.4 because it enables clean
    SPARQL inference without string matching. Both may be present for
    backward compatibility with v0.1-v0.3 data."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range  rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:inferredScheme
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "inferred scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The vocabulary scheme inferred for this FieldClaim, derived
    by the SPARQL CONSTRUCT rule from the DataSource's FieldSchemeUsage
    declaration. Not asserted manually — populated by inference.
    Once inferred, used by SHACL to validate scheme membership without
    requiring explicit skos:inScheme on the concept value."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
    rdfs:range  skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L5.2  sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Source Taxonomy Mapping"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Records how a classification term in a source system's original
    vocabulary maps to the corresponding ATIO taxonomy concept. Preserves the
    original classification even when it does not have a precise ATIO equivalent.
    Enables multi-system taxonomy alignment (CGIAR, IDIA, GARDIAN, partner-specific)."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:hasTaxonomyMapping
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has taxonomy mapping"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mappingSourceSystem
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source system"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Identifier of the source taxonomy system (e.g. 'CGIAR-TRL', 'IDIA-stages', 'GARDIAN')."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceTaxonomyTerm
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source taxonomy term"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The original label or code used in the source system's vocabulary."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:sourceTaxonomyURI
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "source taxonomy URI"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "URI of the source concept, if the source system uses Linked Data."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mappedToATIOConcept
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "mapped to ATIO concept"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The ATIO SKOS concept that corresponds (approximately or exactly) to the source term."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mappingType
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "mapping type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Precision of the correspondence (SKOS mapping vocabulary + sti_atio:noMapping)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:MappingType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mappingField
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "mapped field"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The innovation field to which this taxonomy mapping applies."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:mappingValidatedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "validated by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Curator or KOS specialist who validated this mapping."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
    rdfs:range foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ===========================================================================
#  LAYER 6 -- ACCESS, GOVERNANCE & INTERNAL DATA MANAGEMENT
#  Named graph: sti_atio:graph/internal  (strictly internal)
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L6.1  sti_atio:FieldQA  (per-field quality assessment)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:FieldQA
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Field QA Assessment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A quality assessment record for a specific field on a specific
    innovation. Captures whether the field is complete, AI-generated, curated,
    or flagged for review. Stored in the internal named graph."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:hasFieldQA
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has field QA"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:FieldQA ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:qaField
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "assessed field"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldQA ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:qaStatus
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "QA status"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldQA ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:QAStatus ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:qaAssessedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "QA assessed at"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldQA ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:qaAssessedBy
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "QA assessed by"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldQA ;
    rdfs:range prov:Agent ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:qaNote
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "QA note"@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:FieldQA ;
    rdfs:range rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Record-level QA score
sti_atio:qaScore
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "overall QA score"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Aggregate quality score for the innovation record (0.0-1.0 or 0-100). Now on InnovationRecord (v0.7)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:qaFlag
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "QA flag"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Quality issue flag requiring curator attention."@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:InnovationRecord ;
    rdfs:range sti_atio:QAFlag ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:QAFlag             a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "QA Flag"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "duplicate-suspected | low-completeness | AI-confidence-low | needs-curator-review | rights-unclear"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  L6.2  Named Graph Declarations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  These are documentary declarations; the actual graph management happens
#  in GraphDB via the sparql_entity_storage module configuration.

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#graph/public>
    a sti_atio:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:label "Public KG graph"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Contains all triples for published innovations with accessLevel = public:
    core descriptive properties, taxonomy classifications, family membership,
    bundle relations, geographic data, actor types, impact dimensions.
    Served via the public SPARQL endpoint and JSON-LD / RDF exports."""@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#graph/provenance>
    a sti_atio:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:label "Provenance graph"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Contains the full PROV-O chain (SourceRecord, AIExtractedInnovation,
    FieldClaim, TaxonomyMapping, InnovationVersion, FieldTemporalValue).
    Accessible to internal curators and authorised partner organisations."""@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#graph/internal>
    a sti_atio:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:label "Internal graph"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Contains QA scores, editorial workflow states, collection assignments,
    FieldQA assessments, and curator notes. Strictly internal."""@en .

sti_atio:NamedGraph
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Named Graph"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


# ===========================================================================
#  CONCEPT SCHEME DECLARATIONS
#  Each framework that provides values for sti_atio:readinessLevel or
#  sti_atio:adoptionLevel is declared as a skos:ConceptScheme.
#  Concept instances are managed in VocBench; the schemes are declared
#  here so that the ontology is self-contained and GraphDB can resolve
#  skos:inScheme queries without needing to import a separate vocabulary file.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Readiness / Maturity Schemes ---

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:MaturityScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "CGIAR Scaling Readiness Scale"@en ;
    dcterms:description """9-level scale derived from NASA TRL. Tracks innovations
    from idea (Level 0) to ready-for-scale (Level 9) with evidence-based
    validation at each stage. Standard for CGIAR portfolio management."""@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://scalingreadiness.org> ;
    dcterms:publisher <https://sti-portal.fao.org/orgs/cgiar> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:MaturityScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "IDIA Scaling Stages"@en ;
    dcterms:description """6-stage overlapping continuum from ideation through
    research & development, proof of concept, transition to scale, scaling,
    to sustainable scale. Developed by the International Development Innovation
    Alliance; suited to social, institutional, and policy innovations."""@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.idiaplatform.org> ;
    dcterms:publisher <https://sti-portal.fao.org/orgs/idia> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- Adoption / Uptake Schemes ---

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-adoption>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:AdoptionScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "CGIAR Adoption Scale"@en ;
    dcterms:description """9-level adoption scale measuring the actual spread and
    uptake of an innovation across target user populations."""@en ;
    dcterms:publisher <https://sti-portal.fao.org/orgs/cgiar> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  REPRESENTATIVE CONCEPT INSTANCES
#  (Illustrative; full concept lists are managed in VocBench / GraphDB)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CGIAR TRL concepts (Levels 0–9)
<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-0>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:ReadinessLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 0 -- Idea"@en ;
    skos:notation "TRL-0" ;
    skos:definition "Concept or idea stage; no evidence of feasibility yet."@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-1>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:ReadinessLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 1 -- Research"@en ;
    skos:notation "TRL-1" ;
    skos:broader <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-0> .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-5>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:ReadinessLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 5 -- Controlled testing"@en ;
    skos:notation "TRL-5" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-6>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:ReadinessLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 6 -- Uncontrolled testing"@en ;
    skos:notation "TRL-6" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-7>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:ReadinessLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 7 -- Uncontrolled testing at scale"@en ;
    skos:notation "TRL-7" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-9>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:ReadinessLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-trl> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 9 -- Ready for scaling"@en ;
    skos:notation "TRL-9" .

# IDIA stage concepts
<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-ideation>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ideation"@en ;
    skos:notation "IDIA-1" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-rd>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Research and Development"@en ;
    skos:notation "IDIA-2" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-poc>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Proof of Concept"@en ;
    skos:notation "IDIA-3" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-transition>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Transition to Scale"@en ;
    skos:notation "IDIA-4" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-scaling>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Scaling"@en ;
    skos:notation "IDIA-5" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-sustainable>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:IDIAScalingLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/idia-stages> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sustainable Scale"@en ;
    skos:notation "IDIA-6" .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  CROSS-SCHEME ALIGNMENT MAPPINGS
#  SKOS mapping relations between CGIAR-TRL and IDIA-stages concepts.
#  These are approximate; documented with skos:closeMatch (not exactMatch)
#  because the scales have different evidence requirements and granularity.
#  Full alignment to be validated by KOS specialists in VocBench.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-ideation>
    skos:closeMatch <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-0> ,
                    <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-1> .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-rd>
    skos:closeMatch <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-1> ,
                    <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-5> .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-poc>
    skos:closeMatch <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-5> ,
                    <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-6> .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-transition>
    skos:closeMatch <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-6> ,
                    <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-7> .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-scaling>
    skos:closeMatch <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-7> .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-sustainable>
    skos:closeMatch <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-9> .

# CGIAR adoption concepts (representative)
<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/adoption/cgiar-1>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:AdoptionLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-adoption> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 1 -- Awareness"@en ;
    skos:notation "ADO-1" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/adoption/cgiar-4>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:AdoptionLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-adoption> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 4 -- Early adoption"@en ;
    skos:notation "ADO-4" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/adoption/cgiar-5>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:AdoptionLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-adoption> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 5 -- Significant adoption"@en ;
    skos:notation "ADO-5" .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/adoption/cgiar-9>
    a skos:Concept , sti_atio:AdoptionLevel ;
    skos:inScheme <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/cgiar-adoption> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Level 9 -- Widespread sustained adoption"@en ;
    skos:notation "ADO-9" .

# ===========================================================================
#  INDIVIDUAL CONTROLLED VOCABULARY VALUES
#  (OWL Named Individuals -- manageable as SKOS concepts in VocBench)
# ===========================================================================

# --- Access Levels ---
sti_atio:Public         a sti_atio:AccessLevel ; rdfs:label "Public"@en .
sti_atio:PartnerOnly    a sti_atio:AccessLevel ; rdfs:label "Partner-only"@en .
sti_atio:Internal       a sti_atio:AccessLevel ; rdfs:label "Internal"@en .
sti_atio:Embargoed      a sti_atio:AccessLevel ; rdfs:label "Embargoed"@en .

# --- Curation Status ---
sti_atio:Draft          a sti_atio:CurationStatus ; rdfs:label "Draft"@en .
sti_atio:Staged         a sti_atio:CurationStatus ; rdfs:label "Staged"@en .
sti_atio:Published      a sti_atio:CurationStatus ; rdfs:label "Published"@en .
sti_atio:Archived       a sti_atio:CurationStatus ; rdfs:label "Archived"@en .
sti_atio:FlaggedStatus  a sti_atio:CurationStatus ; rdfs:label "Flagged"@en .

# --- Bundle Types ---
sti_atio:Complementary  a sti_atio:BundleType ; rdfs:label "Complementary"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Innovations that enhance each other when deployed together."@en .
sti_atio:Interdependent a sti_atio:BundleType ; rdfs:label "Interdependent"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Innovations that require each other to function effectively."@en .
sti_atio:Sequential     a sti_atio:BundleType ; rdfs:label "Sequential"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Innovations deployed in sequence in an adoption pathway."@en .
sti_atio:CoCited        a sti_atio:BundleType ; rdfs:label "Co-cited"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Innovations frequently mentioned together in source documents."@en .

# --- Bundle Evidence Types ---
sti_atio:AIDetected          a sti_atio:BundleEvidenceType ; rdfs:label "AI-detected"@en .
sti_atio:CuratorConfirmed    a sti_atio:BundleEvidenceType ; rdfs:label "Curator-confirmed"@en .
sti_atio:PartnerStated       a sti_atio:BundleEvidenceType ; rdfs:label "Partner-stated"@en .
sti_atio:UseCaseOverlap      a sti_atio:BundleEvidenceType ; rdfs:label "Use-case overlap"@en .

# --- Trust Levels ---
sti_atio:TrustedPartner      a sti_atio:TrustLevel ; rdfs:label "Trusted partner"@en .
sti_atio:GeneralSource       a sti_atio:TrustLevel ; rdfs:label "General source"@en .
sti_atio:Unvalidated         a sti_atio:TrustLevel ; rdfs:label "Unvalidated"@en .

# --- Harvesting Methods ---
sti_atio:APIHarvesting       a sti_atio:HarvestingMethod ; rdfs:label "API harvesting"@en .
sti_atio:FileImport          a sti_atio:HarvestingMethod ; rdfs:label "File import"@en .
sti_atio:Scraping            a sti_atio:HarvestingMethod ; rdfs:label "Web scraping"@en .
sti_atio:Crowdsourcing       a sti_atio:HarvestingMethod ; rdfs:label "Crowdsourcing"@en .
sti_atio:ManualEntry         a sti_atio:HarvestingMethod ; rdfs:label "Manual entry"@en .

# --- Family Status ---
sti_atio:FamilyActive        a sti_atio:FamilyStatus ; rdfs:label "Active"@en .
sti_atio:FamilyDeprecated    a sti_atio:FamilyStatus ; rdfs:label "Deprecated"@en .
sti_atio:FamilyProposed      a sti_atio:FamilyStatus ; rdfs:label "Proposed"@en .

# --- Claim Resolution ---
sti_atio:Authoritative       a sti_atio:ClaimResolution ; rdfs:label "Authoritative"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "This claim was selected as the canonical value for the field."@en .
sti_atio:Supplementary       a sti_atio:ClaimResolution ; rdfs:label "Supplementary"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "This claim is retained as additional context but not the canonical value."@en .
sti_atio:Rejected            a sti_atio:ClaimResolution ; rdfs:label "Rejected"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "This claim was assessed as inaccurate or superseded."@en .
sti_atio:PendingReview       a sti_atio:ClaimResolution ; rdfs:label "Pending review"@en .

# --- Field Value Sources ---
sti_atio:FromSourceRecord    a sti_atio:FieldValueSource ; rdfs:label "From source record"@en .
sti_atio:AIGenerated         a sti_atio:FieldValueSource ; rdfs:label "AI-generated"@en .
sti_atio:CuratorAdded        a sti_atio:FieldValueSource ; rdfs:label "Curator-added"@en .
sti_atio:AICurated           a sti_atio:FieldValueSource ; rdfs:label "AI-generated, curator-validated"@en .

# --- Version Triggers ---
sti_atio:NewIngestionRun     a sti_atio:VersionTrigger ; rdfs:label "New ingestion run"@en .
sti_atio:CuratorEdit         a sti_atio:VersionTrigger ; rdfs:label "Curator edit"@en .
sti_atio:AIEnrichmentUpdate  a sti_atio:VersionTrigger ; rdfs:label "AI enrichment update"@en .
sti_atio:MergeEvent          a sti_atio:VersionTrigger ; rdfs:label "Merge event"@en .
sti_atio:SourceUpdate        a sti_atio:VersionTrigger ; rdfs:label "Source content update"@en .

# --- Consent Status ---
sti_atio:ConsentObtained     a sti_atio:ConsentStatus ; rdfs:label "Consent obtained"@en .
sti_atio:ConsentPending      a sti_atio:ConsentStatus ; rdfs:label "Consent pending"@en .
sti_atio:ConsentNA           a sti_atio:ConsentStatus ; rdfs:label "Not applicable"@en .
sti_atio:Anonymised          a sti_atio:ConsentStatus ; rdfs:label "Anonymised"@en .

# --- Merge Strategies ---
sti_atio:AIMerge             a sti_atio:MergeStrategy ;
    rdfs:label "AI merge"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "AI identified the duplicate and merged multiple source records into one extracted entity."@en .
sti_atio:CuratorMerge        a sti_atio:MergeStrategy ;
    rdfs:label "Curator merge"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "One AI-extracted entity per source; curator selected best field values for the published record."@en .


# ===========================================================================
#  ALIGNMENTS TO EXTERNAL VOCABULARIES
#  (Mapping ATIO classes and properties to standard vocabularies)
# ===========================================================================

# ===========================================================================
#  SCHEMA.ORG ALIGNMENTS  (v0.6)
#
#  Design rationale:
#
#  sti_atio:Innovation rdfs:subClassOf schema:Product
#    The most appropriate general alignment. An innovation is a product in
#    the broad schema.org sense: something developed, owned, deployed, and
#    offered in a value chain. This is a universal IS-A relationship that
#    fires automatically for all instances via OWL reasoning.
#    owl:equivalentClass schema:SoftwareApplication (v0.1-v0.5) is replaced:
#    it was too narrow (software only) and too strong (equivalentClass implies
#    every schema:SoftwareApplication is also a sti_atio:Innovation).
#    sti_atio:DigitalInnovation rdfs:subClassOf schema:SoftwareApplication
#    provides the precise alignment for digital subtypes only.
#
#  schema:ProductGroup NOT used for InnovationFamily.
#    schema:ProductGroup describes variants of the same product (size, colour)
#    -- shallow variation. Innovation families group genuinely distinct
#    implementations sharing a mechanism. Semantic mismatch too large.
#    InnovationFamily keeps only schema:Thing as external parent.
#
#  sti_atio:BundleRelation rdfs:subClassOf schema:ProductCollection
#    A bundle is a typed collection of innovations. Loose alignment;
#    sti_atio:BundleRelation retains its own typed properties.
# ===========================================================================

# --- General class alignment ---
sti_atio:Innovation
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:Product ;
    rdfs:comment """Subclass of schema:Product (v0.6, replaces owl:equivalentClass
    schema:SoftwareApplication). Every ATIO innovation is a product in the
    broad schema.org sense. More specific alignments apply to subtypes."""@en .

# --- Innovation subtype alignment ---
sti_atio:DigitalInnovation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Digital Innovation"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:SoftwareApplication ;
    rdfs:comment """Subtype for digital and software-based innovations.
    Aligns to schema:SoftwareApplication. Not all innovations are digital;
    used only when innovationType is in the digital/ICT category."""@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- Bundle alignment ---
sti_atio:BundleRelation
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:ProductCollection ;
    rdfs:comment """Loose alignment to schema:ProductCollection. Declarative
    only; sti_atio:BundleRelation retains its typed properties."""@en .

# --- Property alignments: sti_atio → schema:Product ---

# Ownership / development / funding
sti_atio:ownedBy      rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:brand .
sti_atio:developedBy  rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:manufacturer .
sti_atio:fundedBy     rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:funding .
sti_atio:ownedBy      owl:equivalentProperty dcterms:creator .

# Geography
sti_atio:originCountry  rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:countryOfOrigin .

# Classification
sti_atio:innovationType  rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:category .
sti_atio:thematicArea    rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:category .

# Identity / description
sti_atio:innovationName   owl:equivalentProperty schema:name .
sti_atio:shortDescription owl:equivalentProperty schema:description .
sti_atio:sourceURL        rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:url .
sti_atio:startDate        rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:foundingDate .
sti_atio:implementedBy    rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:provider .

# Planned features: feedback / review loops
# schema:review aligns to planned user/partner feedback on innovations
sti_atio:innovationReview
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "innovation review"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A review or evaluation of this innovation by a user, partner,
    or expert. Planned feature supporting feedback loops in the KB.
    Aligns to schema:review. Range: sti_atio:InnovationReview
    (planned subclass of schema:Review)."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range  schema:Review ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:review ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Planned features: inter-innovation relations
# Untyped loose relation (typed relations use sti_atio:BundleRelation)
sti_atio:relatedInnovation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "related innovation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A loosely related innovation (untyped). Use
    sti_atio:BundleRelation for typed bundle relations. Planned feature
    for 'related innovations' display. Aligns to schema:isRelatedTo."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:isRelatedTo ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Component / part-of relation
sti_atio:componentOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "component of"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """This innovation is a component or prerequisite of a larger
    innovation system or platform. Planned feature. Aligns to schema:isPartOf."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:range  sti_atio:Innovation ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf schema:isPartOf ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# --- InnovationFamily alignment note ---
# schema:ProductGroup NOT used. See design rationale above.
# InnovationFamily retains only schema:Thing as external parent.
sti_atio:InnovationFamily rdfs:comment """No close equivalent in standard
    ontologies. Conceptually analogous to a product family in manufacturing
    ontologies but InnovationFamily groups genuinely distinct implementations,
    not variants of one product. schema:ProductGroup is NOT used (see v0.6
    alignment rationale). Custom class in the sti_atio: namespace."""@en .

# --- DataSource alignments (dcat:Dataset) ---
sti_atio:DataSource rdfs:subClassOf dcat:Dataset .
sti_atio:lastHarvestedAt rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:modified .
sti_atio:sourceAPIEndpoint rdfs:subPropertyOf dcat:endpointURL .

# PROV-O mappings (already declared via rdfs:subClassOf / rdfs:subPropertyOf above)
# Summary of key PROV-O alignments:
#   sti_atio:SourceRecord          rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity
#   sti_atio:AIExtractedInnovation rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity
#   sti_atio:AIEnrichmentActivity  rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity
#   sti_atio:Innovation            NOT prov:Entity (v0.7 -- real-world thing)
#   sti_atio:InnovationRecord      rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity  (NEW v0.7)
#   sti_atio:InnovationVersion     rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity
#   sti_atio:derivedFromSource     rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom
#   sti_atio:derivedFromExtracted  rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom
#   sti_atio:extractedFromSource   rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom
#   sti_atio:extractionActivity    rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasGeneratedBy
#   sti_atio:enrichmentAgent       rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasAssociatedWith
#   sti_atio:inputSourceRecord     rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:used
#   sti_atio:previousVersion       rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasDerivedFrom


# ===========================================================================
#  EXAMPLE INSTANCE DATA  (illustrative; not normative)
# ===========================================================================

# Example: A published innovation with multi-source divergence preserved

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/innovations/I-20241015-00042>
    a sti_atio:Innovation ;
    sti_atio:innovationName "SolarPump Micro-Drip Irrigation System" ;
    sti_atio:shortDescription """Low-cost solar-powered micro-drip irrigation technology
    for smallholder vegetable producers in semi-arid regions of East Africa."""@en ;
    sti_atio:originCountry <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/countries/KEN> ;
    sti_atio:adoptionCountry
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/countries/TZA> ,
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/countries/UGA> ,
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/countries/ETH> ;
    sti_atio:innovationType <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/types/water-management-technology> ;
    sti_atio:innovationStage <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/stages/mature> ;
    sti_atio:useCase <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/use-cases/water-efficient-irrigation> ;
    # Multi-scheme readiness: both CGIAR-TRL and IDIA assessments on one property
    sti_atio:readinessLevel
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-7> ,      # CGIAR TRL-7
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/idia-transition> ;  # IDIA Stage 4
    sti_atio:adoptionLevel  <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/adoption/cgiar-5> ;
    sti_atio:isGrassroots false ;
    sti_atio:accessibility <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/adoptability/medium> ;
    sti_atio:memberOfFamily <https://sti-portal.fao.org/families/F-solar-irrigation> ;
    sti_atio:ownedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/orgs/icrisat> ;
    sti_atio:fundedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/orgs/bmgf> ;
    sti_atio:impactSDG
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/sdgs/sdg-2> ,
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/sdgs/sdg-13> ;
    sti_atio:accessLevel sti_atio:Public ;
    sti_atio:allowAIUpdate true ;
    sti_atio:curationStatus sti_atio:Published ;
    sti_atio:publishedAt "2024-10-15T12:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    sti_atio:lastUpdated "2025-03-22T09:14:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    sti_atio:derivedFromSource
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/source-records/gardian-44210> ,
        <https://sti-portal.fao.org/source-records/technoserve-887> ;
    # Multi-source divergence: readiness level differs between sources
    sti_atio:hasFieldClaim
        [   a sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
            sti_atio:claimField "readinessLevel" ;
            sti_atio:claimRefValue <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-7> ;
            sti_atio:claimedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/source-records/gardian-44210> ;
            sti_atio:claimedAt "2024-10-15T08:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
            sti_atio:curatorResolution sti_atio:Authoritative
        ] ,
        [   a sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
            sti_atio:claimField "readinessLevel" ;
            sti_atio:claimRefValue <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/readiness/cgiar-6> ;
            sti_atio:claimedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/source-records/technoserve-887> ;
            sti_atio:claimedAt "2024-10-15T08:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
            sti_atio:curatorResolution sti_atio:Supplementary ;
            sti_atio:claimResolutionNote "Source uses older CGIAR scale version; GARDIAN value is more recent."@en
        ] ;
    # Taxonomy mapping: TechnoServe uses internal category not in ATIO taxonomy
    sti_atio:hasTaxonomyMapping
        [   a sti_atio:TaxonomyMapping ;
            sti_atio:mappingField "innovationType" ;
            sti_atio:mappingSourceSystem "TechnoServe-internal-v2" ;
            sti_atio:sourceTaxonomyTerm "Solar water lifting" ;
            sti_atio:mappedToATIOConcept <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/types/water-management-technology> ;
            sti_atio:mappingType skos:closeMatch
        ] .

# Example: An Innovation Family
<https://sti-portal.fao.org/families/F-solar-irrigation>
    a sti_atio:InnovationFamily ;
    sti_atio:familyName "Solar-powered irrigation systems"@en ;
    sti_atio:familyDescription """A family of innovations using photovoltaic energy
    to power irrigation pumps and distribution systems for smallholder agriculture."""@en ;
    sti_atio:featureDimensionA <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/mechanisms/solar-photovoltaic> ;
    sti_atio:featureDimensionB <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/themes/water-management> ;
    sti_atio:featureDimensionC <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/actors/smallholder-farmer> ;
    sti_atio:featureDimensionD <https://sti-portal.fao.org/taxonomy/contexts/semi-arid-region> ;
    sti_atio:familyBirthDate "2024-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    sti_atio:familyRegistryVersion "FRv1.0" ;
    sti_atio:familyStatus sti_atio:FamilyActive .

# ===========================================================================
#  SHACL VALIDATION SHAPES
#  Open-world validation: these shapes enforce that concepts used as values
#  of open-range properties belong to a registered scheme.
#  Evaluated by a SHACL processor (e.g. GraphDB SHACL engine, pySHACL).
#  They do NOT constrain the OWL model -- consistent with open-world semantics.
# ===========================================================================

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#shapes/InnovationShape>
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass sti_atio:Innovation ;

    # -- readinessLevel: value must belong to a registered MaturityScheme --
    sh:property [
        sh:path sti_atio:readinessLevel ;
        sh:class skos:Concept ;
        sh:name "readiness level"@en ;
        sh:description """Value must be a skos:Concept whose skos:inScheme
        is typed as sti_atio:MaturityScheme. To use a new framework, declare
        its ConceptScheme as sti_atio:MaturityScheme -- no shape edit needed."""@en ;
        sh:sparql [
            a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
            sh:message """readinessLevel value {$value} does not belong to any
            registered sti_atio:MaturityScheme (checked via skos:inScheme and
            sti_atio:inferredScheme). Declare its ConceptScheme as sti_atio:MaturityScheme,
            or add a FieldSchemeUsage declaration to the DataSource."""@en ;
            sh:select """
                PREFIX sti_atio: <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#>
                PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
                SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                    $this sti_atio:readinessLevel ?value .
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                        # Path 1: concept carries explicit skos:inScheme
                        ?value skos:inScheme ?scheme1 .
                        ?scheme1 a sti_atio:MaturityScheme .
                    }
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                        # Path 2: scheme inferred from DataSource FieldSchemeUsage
                        ?claim a sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
                               sti_atio:claimProperty sti_atio:readinessLevel ;
                               sti_atio:claimRefValue ?value ;
                               sti_atio:inferredScheme ?scheme2 .
                        ?scheme2 a sti_atio:MaturityScheme .
                    }
                }
            """ ;
        ] ;
    ] ;

    # -- adoptionLevel: value must belong to a registered AdoptionScheme ---
    sh:property [
        sh:path sti_atio:adoptionLevel ;
        sh:class skos:Concept ;
        sh:name "adoption level"@en ;
        sh:description """Value must be a skos:Concept whose skos:inScheme
        is typed as sti_atio:AdoptionScheme."""@en ;
        sh:sparql [
            a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
            sh:message """adoptionLevel value {$value} does not belong to any
            registered sti_atio:AdoptionScheme."""@en ;
            sh:select """
                SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                    $this sti_atio:adoptionLevel ?value .
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                        ?value skos:inScheme ?scheme .
                        ?scheme a sti_atio:AdoptionScheme .
                    }
                }
            """ ;
        ] ;
    ] .

# -- How to register a new external framework (documentary example) ---------
#
#  Suppose a partner uses the "XYZ Readiness Scale". To make its concepts
#  valid values of sti_atio:readinessLevel, add only these triples (in their
#  own data file or the shared graph -- no ontology edit):
#
#    <https://partner.example.org/xyz-scale>
#        a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:MaturityScheme ;
#        skos:prefLabel "XYZ Readiness Scale"@en .
#
#    <https://partner.example.org/xyz-scale/level-3>
#        a skos:Concept ;
#        skos:inScheme <https://partner.example.org/xyz-scale> ;
#        skos:prefLabel "Level 3 -- Pilot tested"@en .
#
#  That is the entire registration. The SHACL shape above will immediately
#  accept this scheme's concepts as valid sti_atio:readinessLevel values.
#  Cross-scheme mappings (skos:closeMatch to CGIAR-TRL or IDIA concepts)
#  can be added optionally for navigation and interoperability.

# ===========================================================================
#  SPARQL INFERENCE RULE — scheme derivation  (v0.4)
#
#  This CONSTRUCT rule derives sti_atio:inferredScheme on every FieldClaim
#  from the FieldSchemeUsage declared on its originating DataSource.
#  Run as a scheduled GraphDB CONSTRUCT or a SPARQL Update on the
#  provenance named graph.
#
#  No scheme information needs to be repeated at the individual
#  FieldClaim or innovation property level.  The DataSource record
#  is the single point of truth for "what vocabulary this source uses."
# ===========================================================================

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#rule/InferClaimScheme>
    a sti_atio:SPARQLRule ;
    rdfs:label "Infer FieldClaim scheme from DataSource usage declaration"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """SPARQL CONSTRUCT rule. Run against the provenance named graph.
    For each FieldClaim, find the DataSource it ultimately came from
    (via SourceRecord), look up that source's FieldSchemeUsage for the
    claimed property, and assert sti_atio:inferredScheme on the claim."""@en ;
    sti_atio:sparqlConstruct """
PREFIX sti_atio:  <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#>

CONSTRUCT {
    ?claim sti_atio:inferredScheme ?scheme .
}
WHERE {
    # The claim and its property
    ?claim a sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
           sti_atio:claimProperty  ?prop ;
           sti_atio:claimedBy      ?sourceRecord .

    # Trace back to the DataSource
    ?sourceRecord sti_atio:harvestedFrom ?dataSource .

    # Look up the scheme the DataSource declared for this property
    ?dataSource sti_atio:usesSchemeForField ?usage .
    ?usage sti_atio:forProperty ?prop ;
           sti_atio:usesScheme   ?scheme .
}
""" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:SPARQLRule
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "SPARQL Rule"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A SPARQL CONSTRUCT rule to be executed by the triplestore inference engine."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Fallback rule: also infer from string-based claimField for v0.1-v0.3 data
# that uses claimField (string) rather than claimProperty (URI).
# Requires a mapping from field name string to property URI.
<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#rule/InferClaimSchemeFromString>
    a sti_atio:SPARQLRule ;
    rdfs:label "Infer FieldClaim scheme (string field name fallback)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Fallback SPARQL CONSTRUCT rule for FieldClaim nodes that carry
    sti_atio:claimField (string) instead of sti_atio:claimProperty (URI).
    Requires sti_atio:fieldNameString on each property to bridge string to URI.
    Less efficient than the URI-based rule; migrate to claimProperty when possible."""@en ;
    sti_atio:sparqlConstruct """
PREFIX sti_atio:  <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#>
PREFIX rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

CONSTRUCT {
    ?claim sti_atio:inferredScheme ?scheme .
}
WHERE {
    ?claim a sti_atio:FieldClaim ;
           sti_atio:claimField     ?fieldName ;
           sti_atio:claimedBy      ?sourceRecord .
    ?sourceRecord sti_atio:harvestedFrom ?dataSource .
    ?dataSource sti_atio:usesSchemeForField ?usage .
    ?usage sti_atio:forProperty ?prop ;
           sti_atio:usesScheme   ?scheme .
    # Bridge string field name to property URI via declared label
    ?prop sti_atio:fieldNameString ?fieldName .
}
""" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:fieldNameString
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "field name string"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The Drupal machine name of a field, declared on the corresponding
    sti_atio: property URI. Used by the fallback inference rule to bridge
    string-based claimField values to property URIs.
    Example: sti_atio:readinessLevel sti_atio:fieldNameString 'readinessLevel' ."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Field name string declarations for properties that commonly appear in FieldClaims
sti_atio:readinessLevel sti_atio:fieldNameString "readinessLevel" .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  sti_atio:claimEligible  (v0.5)
#  Marker property on sti_atio: ObjectProperties that reference taxonomy concepts.
#  true  = this field may carry values from different source vocabularies
#          and is therefore FieldClaim-eligible: divergent values from
#          different sources are preserved as FieldClaim nodes rather than
#          overwritten.
#  false = this field is normalised at ingestion to a canonical FAO/ATIO
#          standard vocabulary. No meaningful source divergence exists to
#          preserve; FieldClaim mechanism does not apply.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:claimEligible
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim eligible"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Boolean marker on an sti_atio: ObjectProperty. When true, the
    FieldClaim mechanism applies: values for this property from different
    source records are preserved as sti_atio:FieldClaim nodes, and FieldSchemeUsage
    declarations on the DataSource govern which vocabulary scheme is expected.
    When false, the field is normalised at ingestion (e.g. country names
    harmonised to UN M49 / FAO standard) and FieldClaim is not used."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:range  xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "claim eligibility rationale"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Human-readable explanation of why a property is or is not
    FieldClaim-eligible. Useful for documentation and onboarding."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:range  rdf:langString ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .


sti_atio:adoptionLevel  sti_atio:fieldNameString "adoptionLevel" .
sti_atio:innovationType sti_atio:fieldNameString "innovationType" .
sti_atio:originCountry  sti_atio:fieldNameString "originCountry" .
sti_atio:innovationName sti_atio:fieldNameString "innovationName" .




# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Additional scheme marker classes  (v0.5)
#  Same pattern as sti_atio:MaturityScheme / sti_atio:AdoptionScheme.
#  A skos:ConceptScheme typed as one of these is registered as a valid
#  source of values for the corresponding property.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sti_atio:InnovationTypeScheme
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Type Scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Marker class. A skos:ConceptScheme typed as sti_atio:InnovationTypeScheme
    is registered as a valid source of concepts for sti_atio:innovationType.
    Currently registered: sti_atio:scheme/innovation-types (ATIO native)."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ThematicAreaScheme
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Thematic Area Scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Marker class for sti_atio:thematicArea. Currently registered:
    sti_atio:scheme/afs-themes."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:UseCaseScheme
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Use Case Scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Marker class for sti_atio:useCase. Currently registered:
    sti_atio:scheme/use-cases."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ActorTypeScheme
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Actor Type Scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Marker class for sti_atio:actualUser and sti_atio:prospectiveUser."""@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:InnovationStageScheme
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Innovation Stage Scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

sti_atio:ChallengeScheme
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Challenge Scheme"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio> .

# Register ATIO native schemes
<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/innovation-types>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:InnovationTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "ATIO Innovation Types"@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/afs-themes>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:ThematicAreaScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "ATIO AFS Thematic Areas"@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/use-cases>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:UseCaseScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "ATIO Use Cases"@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/actors>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:ActorTypeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "ATIO Actor Types"@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/innovation-stages>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:InnovationStageScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "ATIO Innovation Stages"@en .

<https://sti-portal.fao.org/ontology/sti-atio#scheme/challenges>
    a skos:ConceptScheme , sti_atio:ChallengeScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "ATIO AFS Challenges"@en .

# ===========================================================================
#  CLAIM ELIGIBILITY DECLARATIONS  (v0.5)
#  Applied to all sti_atio: ObjectProperties that reference taxonomy concepts.
# ===========================================================================

# --- CLAIM-ELIGIBLE (true) ---
# These fields may use different source vocabularies; FieldClaim applies.

sti_atio:readinessLevel
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Multiple readiness frameworks exist
    (CGIAR TRL, IDIA stages, partner-specific scales). Sources use different
    schemes and may assign different levels."""@en .

sti_atio:adoptionLevel
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Multiple adoption scales exist.
    Sources may use different frameworks or assess differently."""@en .

sti_atio:innovationType
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Source databases use heterogeneous
    innovation type taxonomies. Alignment to ATIO types is approximate;
    original source classifications are preserved via FieldClaim."""@en .

sti_atio:innovationStage
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Stage vocabularies vary across sources
    (pre-emergent/emergent/mature vs. source-specific lifecycle terms)."""@en .

sti_atio:thematicArea
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Thematic area classifications differ
    across FAO, CGIAR, and partner taxonomies."""@en .

sti_atio:challengeAddressed
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Challenge taxonomies vary widely
    across source databases."""@en .

sti_atio:useCase
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Use case vocabularies are
    source-specific; ATIO use case taxonomy is ATIO-native."""@en .

sti_atio:innovativeFeature
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Innovative feature classification
    is ATIO-specific; sources rarely use an equivalent vocabulary."""@en .

sti_atio:investmentType
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Investment type taxonomies vary
    across funding and development organisations."""@en .

sti_atio:actualUser
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Actor type taxonomies vary across
    sources; user categories are source-specific."""@en .

sti_atio:prospectiveUser
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Actor type taxonomies vary across
    sources."""@en .

sti_atio:impactSDG
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """SDG mapping is source-assessed;
    different sources may assign different SDGs to the same innovation.
    Note: the SDG concepts themselves are globally standardised (UN URIs),
    but which SDGs a source assigns is a claim, not a fact."""@en .

sti_atio:scalingLevelIDIA
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale "Sub-property of readinessLevel; same rationale."@en .

sti_atio:farmingSystem
    sti_atio:claimEligible true ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Farming system classifications vary
    across FAO, CGIAR, and regional taxonomies."""@en .

# --- NOT CLAIM-ELIGIBLE (false) ---
# These fields are normalised at ingestion; no source divergence to preserve.

sti_atio:originCountry
    sti_atio:claimEligible false ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Normalised at ingestion to UN M49 /
    FAO standard country terms (ISO 3166-1 alpha-3). All source variants
    (country names, codes, alternate spellings) are resolved to the canonical
    FAO concept at extraction time. No FieldClaim needed."""@en .

sti_atio:adoptionCountry
    sti_atio:claimEligible false ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale "Same as originCountry — normalised to FAO standard."@en .

sti_atio:originRegion
    sti_atio:claimEligible false ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Normalised to UN M49 / FAO geographic
    regions at ingestion."""@en .

sti_atio:language
    sti_atio:claimEligible false ;
    sti_atio:claimEligibilityRationale """Normalised to BCP47 / ISO 639 language
    codes at ingestion."""@en .

# ===========================================================================
#  END OF ONTOLOGY
# ===========================================================================
